{"blocks":[["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-22191","Recommendation: STUDY / coexist, don't fork for Logseq",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","obsidian.nvim"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-22255","Rationale: Strong reference for Neovim PKM UX and in-process LSP behavior, but centered on Obsidian semantics.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","obsidian.nvim"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-22377","LogseqLSP",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-22395","Recommendation: STUDY ONLY",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","LogseqLSP"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-22431","Rationale: Stale code plus no detected license is enough to rule out code reuse absent a later license clarification.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","LogseqLSP"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-22554","publish-spa",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-22574","Recommendation: USE AS PUBLISHING ORACLE, not renderer architecture",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","publish-spa"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-22651","Rationale: It is the official file-graph publication path and therefore tells you how Logseq constructs the publishable graph, but it still emits an SPA rather than independently crawlable pages.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","publish-spa"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-22858","old logseq/publish",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-22885","Recommendation: ADAPT rendering ideas",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","old logseq/publish"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-22932","Rationale: Its explicit motivation was to produce static HTML because Logseq's bundled SPA could be slow and SEO-unfriendly—the same problem identified independently.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","old logseq/publish"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-23112","Recommended core decision",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-23144","Ranked implementation paths:",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Recommended core decision"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-23177","First choice: Proposal B",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Recommended core decision"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-23210","Rust engine-first using lsdoc if it survives the real corpus.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Recommended core decision","First choice: Proposal B"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-23432","This gives Rust for the persistence/index/LSP systems work, while outsourcing the parser problem to a project whose stated purpose is precisely to provide a native-Rust, source-aware mldoc equivalent. Tine is evidence that this overall Rust architecture is viable for a real Logseq-compatible application; it already describes a GUI-free Rust core and cached whole-graph reads.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Recommended core decision","First choice: Proposal B"]]],"format_version":5}